Topic 4: Entering the Cell

=== layout: two-panels

# 4. Capacity and Packaging

@left

![adenovirus-packaging figure](assets/set5_gene_therapy/adenovirus_packaging_legacy.jpg)

@right

- The vector genome must be engineered within packaging constraints.
- A larger payload competes with vector sequences and regulatory elements for space.
- Delete replication functions in the vector, then supply needed production functions in controlled producer cells.
- This legacy diagram teaches the design constraint; current products require product-specific manufacturing and safety evidence.

=== layout: one-panel

# 4. When Would You Choose It?

@body

- Pre-existing immunity and treatment-induced immune responses can shorten expression and complicate repeat dosing.
- Innate inflammation can be useful in some vaccine or cancer settings, but it can also limit dose.
- Compare adenovirus with AAV: which one favors larger payload/strong transient expression, and which one favors durable expression in non-dividing cells?
@citation

NHGRI: https://www.genome.gov/genetics-glossary/Gene-Therapy
